Close the product-layer gap on listings + fix several real bugs

Bugs caught and fixed:
- Map labels rendered raw `\u2014` and `\u00b0` escape sequences as
  text (same JSX-text class of bug as the arrows earlier). Switched
  every offending text to interpolated string literals so the chars
  resolve at runtime.
- MarketStats counters momentarily flashed "$0k / 0d / 0%" alongside
  real YoY badges during scroll, which read as broken. Replaced the
  count-up tween with static rendering. The sparkline draw-in is the
  kinetic moment for the block; counting numbers was a SaaS cliche.
- Testimonials AnimatePresence used `mode="wait"`, which created a
  visible blank gap between slides. Removed wait mode and absolute-
  positioned the figure so exit + enter crossfade safely overlap.

Listing cards now earn product depth:
- Favorite-heart button in upper-right (with crimson active state and
  proper aria-pressed). Lives in `ListingCardChrome.tsx` as a client
  island so the surrounding plates can stay server-rendered.
- Price-per-sqft displayed beside the asking price, italic serif so
  it reads as a quiet annotation, not another bold number.
- Hover-reveal "Schedule a tour" affordance slides up from the
  bottom edge of the image. Pure CSS group-hover, no JS.
- Dropped the literal "Plate" word from the meta strip (just the
  italic plate number now). User feedback: the word was noise on
  scannable cards.

Strengthened conversion paths:
- Hero CTA promoted from outline to filled crimson with shadow lift.
  It's the loudest moment on the hero now, instead of the quietest.
- SearchBar reintroduced as its own dedicated editorial section
  between Manifesto and MarketStats. Real shape (intent + city +
  beds + price), serif inputs, hairline rules, one big crimson
  submit. Lives apart from the hero so it doesn't crowd the headline
  and gets the breathing room to feel like a deliberate product
  moment, not a Zillow widget.

Same plate vocabulary now in FeaturedListings (server async),
ListingsCatalog (client), and RelatedListings (server async) so all
three surfaces read as one system.
